  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np6:3.1.6": "For an explanation of this, see comment at [pli-tv-bu-vb-np4:2.1.6](). ",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np6:3.1.7": "",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np6:3.1.8": "_Agāraṁ_ is typically rendered as “in a house”. The problem with this is that it is not unallowable for a monastic to live in a building that is the equivalent of a house. What a monastic should not do is own a home and then live there. ",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np6:3.1.9": "",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np6:3.1.10": "",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np6:3.1.11": "",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np6:3.1.12": "The six are linen, cotton, silk, wool, sunn hemp, and hemp; see [pli-tv-kd8:3.1.6](). According to [pli-tv-kd8:21.1.4](), the size referred to here is no smaller than 8 by 4 _sugataṅgula_, “standard fingerbreadths”. For an explanation of the idea of _vikappanā_, see Appendix of Technical Terms. For the rendering of _cīvara_ as “robe-cloth”, see the same appendix. ",
